{"id": "EUVD-2026-80450", "enisaUuid": "30258f6e-c811-351b-a4be-ac47618af083", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nscsi: qla2xxx: Don't query firmware state while chip is down\n\nqla2x00_fw_state_show() initializes rval to QLA_FUNCTION_FAILED and jumps\nto the out: label when the chip is down or EEH is busy. The out: block\nthen re-issued qla2x00_get_firmware_state() because rval != QLA_SUCCESS,\ndefeating the chip-down/EEH-busy guards and issuing a mailbox command\n(outside optrom_mutex) during ISP reset or PCI error recovery, which can\nhang the adapter. It also turned a normal in-lock mailbox failure into a\nsecond unsynchronized mailbox attempt.\n\nMake the out: fallback only mark the firmware state as unknown. The\nmailbox is now issued at most once, inside optrom_mutex, and only when\nthe chip is up and not EEH-busy.", "datePublished": "2026-09-16T10:31:24", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:53:43", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/178d984e8875292582e4295cf559b2b11d3c9325", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cba780c01f72f8585ca81ad7304097f8b12ef339", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/22f44f77da496bc355479c08a0a9dbc9ad42ba42", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b6a30baa29695fa0eaba4a3a04435a3c1a5cb63d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7bc2baed8a3d6a1e2a3f6b78d245f25d1e18a749", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a194684853dceaa1d6b7a9a02bc12f479232ad9b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a6374b508893de15fee78583a95f5099d7812e85", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e0cebe20dcffbed9c078fe30e2d18cd5046d9eff"], "aliases": ["GHSA-52m9-92gj-jg2v", "CVE-2026-89850"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "044c4a51-348e-3826-8b25-90af74cfc64f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b6faaaf796d7bfb00e32ca5c905d55cc43e89448 <22f44f77da496bc355479c08a0a9dbc9ad42ba42"}, {"id": "10bc032e-0473-3d02-84d3-9ff91e533fec", "product": {"name": "Linu